# KEUR-DOC-004 — agent-tool file is a divergent copy, not a pointer to AGENTS.md (shim divergence).
# @implements ADR-061 (shims by reference, never by copy)
#
# max-lines engine with a LOW budget: a per-tool instruction file (CLAUDE.md,
# .cursorrules, copilot-instructions.md) should be a symlink or a one-line
# pointer to the single source, AGENTS.md (ADR-061). If it is more than a few
# lines, it is a divergent copy — a second source that will drift from AGENTS.md
# the moment one is edited and the other is not.
#
# A symlink is not read as content here (it resolves to AGENTS.md), so this
# fires only on a real, fat copy. Budget 10 lines: enough for a pointer with a
# short note, far too few for a forked copy. WARN — the fix is "make it a
# pointer", not a gate.
#
# NOTE: .cursorrules has no extension; filenames match covers it. The GitHub
# copilot file lives at .github/copilot-instructions.md — basename match.
id: KEUR-DOC-004
ilities: [modifiability]
maturity: 2
title: Agent-tool file is a copy, not a pointer to AGENTS.md (shim divergence)
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: max-lines
action: warn
min_count: 10
target:
  filenames: CLAUDE.md .cursorrules copilot-instructions.md GEMINI.md .windsurfrules
patterns:
  - regex: ""
    message: "This agent-tool file is longer than a pointer, so it is a divergent copy of AGENTS.md — a second source that will drift (ADR-061). Make it a symlink to AGENTS.md, or a one-line 'See AGENTS.md' stub. Keep one editable source for agent instructions."
confidence: 0.6
fix: "Replace the copy with 'ln -s AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md' where symlinks are honoured, or a one-line pointer file ('See [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md)') on locked-down endpoints where symlinks are blocked. Never maintain N copies."
